private static class Node<T> {
                                    // Generic linked list node
  Node<T> next;
                                    // Reference to next node
  T element;
                                    // Reference to an element
  Node(T elem) {
                                    // Construct a new node that
    element = elem;
                                    // references elem of type T
    next = null;
  }
}

slides.raw_text:
The Node<T> class
❑Node<T> is defined as private static class nested under 
LinkedStack<T> for better grouping and encapsulation.
❑It serves as the node containing a reference to the next node 
and a reference to the generic element of type T.
private static class Node<T> { 
// Generic linked list node
  Node<T> next; 
// Reference to next node
  T element; 
// Reference to an element
  Node(T elem) { 
// Construct a new node that
    element = elem; 
// references elem of type T
    next = null;
  }
}

