slides.raw_text:
The pop method
❑The pop() method removes the top node and returns a 
reference to its element. If the stack is empty, then a 
RuntimeException is thrown.
public T pop() throws RuntimeException {
  if (isEmpty()) throw new RuntimeException("Stack is empty");
  Node<T> next = top.next; 
// Reference to next node
  T element = top.element; 
// Reference to top element
  top.next = null; 
// Disconnect top node
  top = next; 
// top now references next node
  count--; 
// Decrement count of elements
  return element; 
// Reference to popped element
}

